gestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"* Simple obesity of the heart."},{"label":"B","text":"Fatty dystrophy of myocardium."},{"label":"C","text":"Ischemic heart disease."},{"label":"D","text":"Hypertension"},{"label":"E","text":"Acute myocardium infarct"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6e7d92eb810b","stem":"During dissection of a 65 year old patient, who suffered from a fibrous- cavernous tuberculosis, an enlarged, dense spleen was found. Spleen section gross- ly had brown-pinkish color, smooth, waxy-like surface. Which pathological process listed below is the most credible?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"* Sebaceous spleen."},{"label":"B","text":"Glazed spleen."},{"label":"C","text":"Porphyry spleen."},{"label":"D","text":"Sago spleen."},{"label":"E","text":"Cyanotic induration"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a19bd18dd64c","stem":"A post mortem performed on a 50 year old male who died of a heart attack indi- 9 cated a symmetric type of obesity of the III degree with rupture of the walls of the right ventricle and hemopericardium. Under the epicardium surplus deposits of fat were found. Microscopically, fatty tissue from the epicardium was dispersed in the myocardium with an atrophy of the muscle fibers. Which process listed below is the most reliable?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Obesity the heart."},{"label":"B","text":"Fatty dystrophy of myocardium."},{"label":"C","text":"Acute infarct of myocardium."},{"label":"D","text":"Ischemic heart disease."},{"label":"E","text":"Hypertension."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-5b960c28ba33","stem":"An autopsy of a 45-year-old female revealed the kidneys were dense, yellow in color and appear to have a greasy brilliance. Which pathological process is most likely?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Amyloidosis"},{"label":"B","text":"Hyalinosis"},{"label":"C","text":"Fatty dystrophy"},{"label":"D","text":"Mucoid swelling"},{"label":"E","text":"Hemochromatosis"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ced0f3aafd51","stem":"Macroscopic examination of a stomach delivered from surgery, revealed a round lesion 1.5cm in diameter which extended by the muscle layer at the antral zone of a small curvature. A semilucent dense area on the bottom of the defect was also determined. It resembled hyaline cartilage. Which process developed in the bottom of the stomach lesion?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Abdomen","topicOriginal":"Abdomen","subtopic":"Stomach","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Localized hyalinosis"},{"label":"B","text":"Amyloidosis"},{"label":"C","text":"Mucoid swelling"},{"label":"D","text":"Fibrinoid changes"},{"label":"E","text":"Generalized hyalinosis"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Abdomen","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5b82c1443dff","stem":"A skin biopsy of a patient with allergic vasculitis was submitted for examina- tion. It is discovered that the vessel walls were thickened and homogeneous. Picro- fuxin stained a tissues a yellow color. They were Shiff-positive. Which pathologi- cal process developed in the walls of the vessels?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Fibrinoid swelling"},{"label":"B","text":"Amyloidosis"},{"label":"C","text":"Mucoid swelling"},{"label":"D","text":"Hyalinosis"},{"label":"E","text":"Lipidosis"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2a494568b053","stem":"The post-mortem of a patient revealed feature of chronic kidney insufficiency. Grossly, kidneys were enlarged, dense, wax-like, with foci of irregular depressed scars on their surface. Microscopically, the mesangeal areas were expanded and the glomerular capillaries obstructed by Congo red stain-positive amorphous acellular material. In some sections the deposits took on nodular appearance. Which of the following diagnoses is most reliable? 10","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Amyloidosis of the kidneys (Amyloid nephropathy)"},{"label":"B","text":"Acute glomerulonephritis"},{"label":"C","text":"Chronic glomerulonephritis"},{"label":"D","text":"Subacute glomerulonephritis"},{"label":"E","text":"Lipoid nephrosis"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-34b0a09e9566","stem":"At autopsy a 76-year-old male, with a history of peritonitis 10 years ago, is found to have thickened and dense both liver and spleen capsules. They were trans- lucent on a sectional view. What is the most likely pathology of the described or- gans capsules?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Hyalinosis."},{"label":"B","text":"Necrosis."},{"label":"C","text":"Mucoid swelling."},{"label":"D","text":"Fibrinoid swelling."},{"label":"E","text":"Amyloidosis."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6ff6d4c94a86","stem":"A 55-year-old female, with a long history of rheumatoid arthritis, develops ren- al failure and dies. An autopsy revealed an enlarged solid spleen. On the sectional view, its tissue had brown-reddish coloring with enlarged follicles that look like translucent grayish-white grains. What is the most likely pathological process?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Sago spleen."},{"label":"B","text":"Frosted spleen."},{"label":"C","text":"Lardaceous spleen."},{"label":"D","text":"Spleen hyalinosis."},{"label":"E","text":"Porphyry spleen."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2d947eb3d9ea","stem":"A 66-year-old female, with a long history of post-traumatic osteomyelitis, is admitted to the hospital for treatment of nephrotic syndrome. On the night pf ad- mission she suddenly dies. Autopsy revealed dense, white kidneys with scars in the cortical layer; they had a sebaceous glow on the cut surface. What is the most likely kidneys pathology?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Secondary amyloidosis."},{"label":"B","text":"Primary amyloidosis. С. Idiopathic amyloidosis."},{"label":"D","text":"Chronic glomerulonephritis."},{"label":"E","text":"Chronic pyelonephritis."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3012da81c060","stem":"A 55-year-old man, with a long history of a symmetrical type of severe obesity, developed acute heart insufficiency followed with lethal outcome. An autopsy re- vealed right ventricle wall burst with hemopericardium and excessive amount of fatty tissue under epicardium. Microscopically: adipose tissue from epicardium penetrates myocardium with muscle fibers atrophy. Name the pathological process?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Simple fatty heart."},{"label":"B","text":"Fatty degeneration of myocardium."},{"label":"C","text":"Ischemic disease."},{"label":"D","text":"Essential hypertension."},{"label":"E","text":"Acute myocardial infarction. 11"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-f7eb1f67948b","stem":"An autopsy of a 56-year-old man with cavernous tuberculosis of the lungs re- vealed enlarged dense spleen. The cut surface of the spleen tissue had brown-red, smooth, and wax-like appearance. Which of the following is the most likely pa- thology in the spleen?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"* Lardaceous spleen. ."},{"label":"B","text":"Glaze spleen."},{"label":"C","text":"Porphyric spleen."},{"label":"D","text":"Sago spleen."},{"label":"E","text":"Cyanotic induration."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7c567f7d08f0","stem":"A patient had been suffering from bronchoectases for a long time and died of uremia. Autopsy revealed enlarged, dense kidneys with greasy cut surfaces. Which of the following was the most likely disease?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Renal amyloidosis."},{"label":"B","text":"Glomerulonephritis."},{"label":"C","text":"Acute tubular necrosis."},{"label":"D","text":"Pyelonephritis."},{"label":"E","text":"Nephosclerosis Mixed dystrophy"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b865e2bd174b","stem":"The necrotic Peyer‘s patches of the ileum from the patient with typhoid fever are stained in a yellow-brown color. Which pigment impregnates the necrotic tissue?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"labe