l":"B","text":"̳Hairy‘ heart"},{"label":"C","text":"Solder plaque (bony heart)"},{"label":"D","text":"Tiger‘s heart ( ̳tabby cat‘)"},{"label":"E","text":"Bovine heart"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-215d5483a3cd","stem":"A man with insufficiency of the mitral valve complained of a cough and sputum with a brownish colouring. Which pigment results in this color of the sputum? 12","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Hemosiderin"},{"label":"B","text":"Melanin С. Hemoglobin"},{"label":"D","text":"Hemomelanin"},{"label":"E","text":"Iron sulfate"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-8d99a2f7f87a","stem":"The post-mortem of a man who presented in the hospital with a history of a snakebite reveals expressed intravessels hemolysis. During dissection it is noted that the spleen, bone marrow and lymphatic nodes had a brown colouring. Micro- scopic examination showed that the cytoplasm of macrophages got a brown pig- ment. Which pigment accumulated in the tissues?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Abdomen","topicOriginal":"Abdomen","subtopic":"Spleen","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"* Hemosiderin"},{"label":"B","text":"Hematoidin"},{"label":"C","text":"Hematin"},{"label":"D","text":"Lipofuscin"},{"label":"E","text":"Bilirubin."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Abdomen","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9c91b7a0c009","stem":"The dissection of a patient who suffered from rheumatism and chronic rheumatic valvulitis revealed that mitral valve leaflet was thickened with rough stony depo- sits. Name the pathology presented with stony appearance of the valves?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"* Dystrophy calcification"},{"label":"B","text":"Metastatic calcification"},{"label":"C","text":"Metabolic calcification."},{"label":"D","text":"Fibrinoid"},{"label":"E","text":"Amyloidosis."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-04122c864518","stem":"An endoscopy was performed on a patient with a chronic stomach ulcer compli- cated with hemorrhage. This procedure revealed a brownish (coffee-like) liquid in the stomach. Which pigment results in the color of the stomach contents?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"* Hematin hydrochloride"},{"label":"B","text":"Hemosiderin"},{"label":"C","text":"Bilirubin"},{"label":"D","text":"Ferritin"},{"label":"E","text":"Porphyrin"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ce2dbe5f14b7","stem":"A 46-year-old man has an acute stomach ulcer complicated by gastric bleeding and vomiting. Gastric masses had a brown color and ―coffee-like‖ appearance. Which pigment created such colouring?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"* Hematin hydrochloride"},{"label":"B","text":"Hemoglobin"},{"label":"C","text":"Bilirubin"},{"label":"D","text":"Hemomelanin"},{"label":"E","text":"Iron sulfide"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-26dafee777fe","stem":"A 66-year-old patient complained of pain in the hands and feet joints. Physical examination revealed a deformation and painful of the joints. Laboratory tests showed the increased level of uric acid salts in the blood and urine. Which one of following is not being fully metabolized? 13","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Ear","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Nucleoprotein."},{"label":"B","text":"Calcium."},{"label":"C","text":"Chromoprotein."},{"label":"D","text":"Lipoprotein."},{"label":"E","text":"Potassium."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-ea06d26a56de","stem":"A man died from chronic sepsis. A post-mortem revealed an atrophy of the ske- letal muscles and brown atrophy of both myocardium and liver. Which one of the following pigments accumulated in tissues?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Abdomen","topicOriginal":"Abdomen","subtopic":"Liver","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Lipofuscin"},{"label":"B","text":"Lipochrome С. Hemosiderin"},{"label":"D","text":"Hemomelanin"},{"label":"E","text":"Melanin"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Abdomen","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a9db40d17af2","stem":"A 58-year-old male has been ill for many years with leukemia. A post-mortem exposed a brown color in the marrow, spleen, liver, and lymphatic nodes. The Perls‘ histochemical reaction was conducted. It was determined that the reticular, the endothelial cells and histiocytes of these organs contained granules of a dark blue color. Which pigment is responsible for the colouring?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Hemosiderin"},{"label":"B","text":"Bilirubin"},{"label":"C","text":"Hematoidin"},{"label":"D","text":"Hemomelanin"},{"label":"E","text":"Hematoporphyrin"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-fd415ce2723a","stem":"The post-mortem of a patient who suffered from malaria revealed jaundiced skin, sclera and mucous membranes. Also, the spleen was enlarged and had dark- grey color. This colour of the spleen is due to the presence of","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Hemomelanin"},{"label":"B","text":"Hemosiderin"},{"label":"C","text":"Lipofuscin"},{"label":"D","text":"Melanin"},{"label":"E","text":"Hemoporphyrin"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic","subject_suggestion_available"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_suggestion_available","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-08ace6ed6f21","stem":"A 56 year old patient died from chronic cardiac insufficiency as a result of rheumatic heart-disease. A post-mortem revealed that lungs were enlarged, dense with red-brownish coloring. What is the most likely diagnosis?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Brown induration lungs"},{"label":"B","text":"Acute bronchitis"},{"label":"C","text":"Honey-comb lungs"},{"label":"D","text":"Chronic bronchitis"},{"label":"E","text":"Chronic emphysema"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-591b4c63716e","stem":"A patient with mitral valve insufficiency presents in his sputum cells, filled with brown pigment. The Perls‘ reaction is positive. Name this pigment.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Hemosiderin"},{"label":"B","text":"Hematoidin 14"},{"label":"C","text":"Melanin"},{"label":"D","text":"Porphyrin"},{"label":"E","text":"Bilirubin"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-fbd78caf047b","stem":"A 66-year-old male, with a history of hematogenic tuberculosis was examined. This revealed hyperpigmentation of skin and mucous membranes, cachexia and insufficiency of the cardio-vascular system. Which disease caused such changes?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Respiratory Medicine","topicOriginal":"Respiratory Medicine","subtopic":"Tuberculosis","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Addison‘s disease"},{"label":"B","text":"Phaeochromocytoma"},{"label":"C","text":"Simmond‘s disease"},{"label":"D","text":"Cushing disease"},{"label":"E","text":"Greves‘ disease"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Respiratory Medicine","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-455663372fdc","stem":"A 52-year-old male with a history of sub-acute septic endocarditis is examined by a physician. A doctor revealed marked general pallor with icteric skin, sclera and visible mucous membranes. Blood test showed accumulation of indirect react- ing bilirubin (unconjugated bilirubin). The yellow staining of the skin, sclera and mucous membranes indicates which one of the following?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Prehepatic jaundice"},{"label":"B","text":"Fatty dystrophy"},{"label":"C","text":"Hemosiderosis"},{"label":"D","text":"Hepatic jaundice"},{"label":"E","text":"Posthepatic jaundice"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ef1053910ba5","stem":"A 62-year-old female with a history of stomach cancer with plural metastases died from a cachexia. Select the characteristic changes of the heart expected to be revealed on dissection.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Brown atrophy of myocardium."},{"label":"B","text":"Amyloid cardiomegaly."},{"label":"C","text":"Dilatation cardiomyopathy."},{"label":"D","text":"Hypertrophy cardiomyopathy."},{"label":"E","text":"―Tabby cat‖ (\"Tiger‘s heart\")."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0852df21bdd3","stem":"A patient developed a cyst in the cerebrum following a hemorrhagic stroke. Two years later the patient died from pneumonia due to a complication of influen- za. During examination of the brain cyst it is noted that the walls have a rusty tint. Perls‘ reaction is positive. Name the process occurring in the wall of the cyst?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Neurology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Localized hemosiderosis"},{"label":"B","text":"General hemosiderosis"},{"label":"C","text":"Local hemomelanosis"},{"label":"D","text":"Infiltration of bilirubin"},{"label":"E","text":"Primary haemochromatosis"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Neurology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-74c85457ea95","stem":"A patient with a long history of tuberculosis was examined at the hospital. Physical examination revealed a grayish-brown skin color, lowered arterial pres- sure, hypodynamia and a decline of the level of 17-oxycorticosteroids in the urine and blood plasma. A problem with the metabolism of which pigment is indicated by the clinical signs of this patient? 15","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Medical Biochemistry","topic":"Metabolism · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Metabolism","options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Melanin"},{"label":"B","text":"Bilirubin"},{"label":"C","text":"Lipofuscin"},{"label":"D","text":"Lipochrome"},{"label":"E","text":"Hemosiderin"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Medical Biochemistry","displayTopic":"Metabolism · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-39d52e1a113b","stem":"A fragment of skin (1х2 centimeters) delivered for histological research. Gross- ly a small (0,5 cm in diameter) slightly elevated brown lesion, sharply demarcated from the surrounding normal skin, was recognized. Microscopically, a lesion pre- sented with nevus cells nests, rich with brown pigment. This pigment had negative Perls‘ reaction. Name the pigment.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Melanin"},{"label":"B","text":"Hematoidin"},{"label":"C","text":"Hemosiderin"},{"label":"D","text":"Bilirubin"},{"label":"E","text":"Hemomelanin"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"