rtem was performed on a 55-year-old male, who over last eight years suffered from chronic form of malaria. At the dissection both grey matter of the cerebrum and a spleen had the ash-grey color. Which pigment is responsible for this discoloration?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Hemomelanin"},{"label":"B","text":"Lipofuscin"},{"label":"C","text":"Hematoporphyrin"},{"label":"D","text":"Melanin"},{"label":"E","text":"Hemosiderin"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-242fb4b074fe","stem":"A 62-year-old male who has been ill with diabetes mellitus for 15 years died from a cerebral hemorrhage. Post-mortem revealed kidneys diminished in size with 16 a fine-grained surface. The epithelium of the canaliculi of distal nephron‘s segment was high, with a light foamy cytoplasm. The Best‘s carmine staining demonstrated a bright red coloring of the cytoplasm‘s accumulations. These changes in the epi- thelium resulted from the accumulation of","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Glycogen"},{"label":"B","text":"Lipids"},{"label":"C","text":"Hyaline"},{"label":"D","text":"Proteins"},{"label":"E","text":"Amyloid"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unveri