 history of secondary syphilis, has noticed foci of the skin depigmentation at his neck. Name the pathological process of the skin.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Leukoderma."},{"label":"B","text":"Metaplasia."},{"label":"C","text":"Leukoplakia."},{"label":"D","text":"Dysplasia."},{"label":"E","text":"Parakeratosis."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2b48a1074df2","stem":"a 38-year old female is found to have bilateral adrenal adenopathy resulted in brownish coloring of her skin. Perls' test of her skin‘s biopsy was negative. What pigment altered the color of the skin?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Melanin."},{"label":"B","text":"Hemosiderin."},{"label":"C","text":"Porphyrin."},{"label":"D","text":"Lipofuscin."},{"label":"E","text":"Biliverdin."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-cd905d6490c5","stem":"A 70-year-old man has noticed recent swelling of joints of his hands and feet. Joints are painful and stiff. Laboratory tests revealed an increased level of urates in blood and urine. What is the most likely substance caused described pathology?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Ear","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Nucleoproteins."},{"label":"B","text":"Calcium."},{"label":"C","text":"Chromoproteids."},{"label":"D","text":"Lipoproteins."},{"label":"E","text":"Potassium. 18"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-0bb56fea6991","stem":"A 70 year-old male with a history of chronic shigellosis died. At post-mortem tissue samples were collected for histopoly. Microscopic investigation of hematoxylyn and eosin slides revealed amorphous violet deposits in stroma of the heart, kidneys, lungs and stomach mucosa. Koss' reaction was positive. What is the most likely pathological developed?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Metastatic calcification."},{"label":"B","text":"Dystrophic calcification."},{"label":"C","text":"Metabolic calcification."},{"label":"D","text":"Amyloidosis."},{"label":"E","text":"Hyalinosis."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3775ad59053f","stem":"A woman presented to intensive care department with symptoms of severe he- molysis due to a snake bite. An autopsy revealed brown coloration of the spleen, bone marrow, and lymph nodes. Microscopic examination showed the accumula- tion of brown pigment in cytoplasm of macrophages of tissue sampler. Which of the following is the pigment that was accumulated in the tissues?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Abdomen","topicOriginal":"Abdomen","subtopic":"Spleen","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Hemosiderin"},{"label":"B","text":"Hematoidin."},{"label":"C","text":"Hematin"},{"label":"D","text":"Lipofuscin."},{"label":"E","text":"Bilirubin."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Abdomen","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-fbf99a90e0c2","stem":"A patient with prolonged esophageal carcinoma died of cachexy. An autopsy revealed atrophy of his heart and liver, marked reduction of subcutaneous and re- troperitoneal fatty tissue. Microscopical examination revealed accumulations of the golden-brown granules and clumps with negative Prussian blue reaction within the myocardial fibers. Which of the following pigments accumulated in myocardial fibers?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Ear","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"*Lipofuscin."},{"label":"B","text":"Melanin."},{"label":"C","text":"Hematoidin."},{"label":"D","text":"Ferritin."},{"label":"E","text":"Hemomelanin. Necrosis. Postmortem changes."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"c