ified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5c0b2d9377cc","stem":"A 63-year-old male died of an endemic typhus. During the post-mortem it was revealed that the muscles of the abdominal wall and legs were dense with whitish- yellowish colouring. They resemble a candle. Name the pathological process? А. *Waxy necrosis (Zenker‘s necrosis)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Apoptosis"},{"label":"C","text":"Fibrinoid necrosis"},{"label":"D","text":"Colliquative necrosis"},{"label":"E","text":"Caseous necrosis"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-83d1711764d5","stem":"A 72-year-old-male had an infarct of the dextral hemisphere of the brain. One year later a computer tomography of the right hemisphere of the brain reveals a cavity with smooth walls and filled with liquid. Which pathological process is he most likely to have? А. *Post-infarct cyst","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Hydrocephalus"},{"label":"C","text":"Grey softening of a brain"},{"label":"D","text":"Infarct of a brain"},{"label":"E","text":"Hematoma"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6631066b2751","stem":"A post-mortem revealed a thrombus in the left artery mesencephalicae and a large locus of grey softening in the tissues of the left hemisphere of a brain. Which pathological process is most likely to be present in the brain? А. * Ischemic infarct","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Neuroanatomy","topicOriginal":"Neuroanatomy","subtopic":"Brain","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Coagulative necrosis"},{"label":"C","text":"Abscess"},{"label":"D","text":"Moist gangrene"},{"label":"E","text":"Sequestrum"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Neuroanatomy","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-94902d316307","stem":"At a post-mortem of the 46-year-old male a large yellow - grey lesion was found in the left ventricle of the heart. A fresh thrombus was found in the coronary artery. What disease is he most likely to have? А. *Infarct of the myocardium","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Cardiosclerosis"},{"label":"C","text":"Myocarditis"},{"label":"D","text":"Amyloidosis"},{"label":"E","text":"Cardiomyopathy 20"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-47d306f360e2","stem":"At autopsy a 60-year-old male is found to have ischemic heart disease and athe- rosclerosis of the coronary arteries of heart. A section of the myocardium showed a white-yellowish focus, surrounded by the zone of hemorrhages in the apex, anterior and lateral walls areas of a left ventricle. Which is the most likely diagnosis? А. *Infarct of the myocardium","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Post-infarction cardiosclerosis"},{"label":"C","text":"Diffuse cardiosclerosis"},{"label":"D","text":"Myocarditis"},{"label":"E","text":"Fatty dystrophy of the myocardium"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b0159b9f5e6b","stem":"After a long staying in the bed a patient with circulatory deficiency got the skin and soft tissue darening above the sacrums. These tissues became swallowed. Sloughing off the epidermis in this area resulted in ulceration. Which complication is most likely? А. *Decubitus ulcer","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Dry gangrene"},{"label":"C","text":"Phlegmon"},{"label":"D","text":"Infarct"},{"label":"E","text":"Abscess"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-154413116994","stem":"Histological investigation of liver‘s biopsy revealed that some cells burn on small pieces with separate organellas and nuclei fragments surrounded by a mem- brane. The inflammatory reaction was missing. Select pathological process, the described changes are characteristic for: А. *Apoptosis","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Necrosis"},{"label":"C","text":"Karyorrhexis"},{"label":"D","text":"Plasmolysis"},{"label":"E","text":"Plasmorrhexis"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a51cdd03dfa1","stem":"A male who had a long history of the intermittent claudication demonstrates the tissue of the foot fingers as being dry with a black colour, resembling a mummy. On small interval from this place the dichromatic line (red colour is next to un- changed tissues, and white - yellow colour close to a tered tissues). Which type of a necrosis occurred? А. *Gangrene.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Infarct."},{"label":"C","text":"Sequester."},{"label":"D","text":"Decubitus ulcer."},{"label":"E","text":"Maceration."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f030430ceb0b","stem":"A 62-year-old male got a surgery due to the inguinal hernia. Macroscopic ex- amination reveals that the wall of the intestine was a cyanotic, inflated, swallowed and coated with threads of a fibrin. Peristalsis was not heard. Which pathological process occurred in the wall of the intestine? А. * Moist gangrene.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Abdominal Surgery · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Abdominal Surgery","options":[{"label":"B","text":"Dry gangrene. 21"},{"label":"C","text":"Coagulate necrosis"},{"label":"D","text":"Colliquative necrosis"},{"label":"E","text":"Decubitus ulcer"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Abdominal Surgery · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-4d1af1d18ac1","stem":"A postmortem of a man, who died from typhoid revealed muscles on the abdo- minal wall and legs were dense, fragile, whitish-yellowish colour, resembling a candle. Which term best characterizes the muscles changes? А. *Zenker‘s necrosis","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb","topicOriginal":"Lower Limb","subtopic":"Leg","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Fibrinoid necrosis"},{"label":"C","text":"Caseous necrosis"},{"label":"D","text":"Colliquative necrosis"},{"label":"E","text":"Apoptosis"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6c87623ae5bc","stem":"A 48-year-old male, who had a history of hypertension for 12 years, present acute disturbance of the cerebral circulation. He developed a headache and altera- tion of the motion in the right extremity. Following right-handed hemiplegia re- sulted in fatal outcome. A postmortem revealed a systemic hyalinosis of the small arteries, thrombosis in the left arteria cerebri media. In the left parietal-temporal area a lesion was found, which is called: А. *Ischemic infarct","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Hemorrhage"},{"label":"C","text":"Abscess of a brain"},{"label":"D","text":"Hemorrhagic infarct"},{"label":"E","text":"Edema of the brain"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-50aaf1adb6f8","stem":"A 45-year-old male suddenly died with the following findings revealed during the postmortem. In the back wall of the left ventricle of the heart a myocardial in- farction was found. Which of the following microscopic changes in the myocardi- ocytes can be seen in the locus of an infarct? А. *Karyolysis","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Fatty dystrophy"},{"label":"C","text":"Carbohydrate dystrophy"},{"label":"D","text":"Calcification"},{"label":"E","text":"Protein dystrophy"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ba41f04ccf69","stem":"A postmortem of on a previously ill 48-year-old patient found an obturation of the lumen of the middle cerebral artery due to a thrombus. In the parietal-temporal area of the left hemisphere of the brain a locus of grey colour tissue with soft tex- ture is found. Which tern best characterizes the brain tissue changes? А. *Infarct","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Ear","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Sequester"},{"label":"C","text":"Gangrene"},{"label":"D","text":"Caseous necrosis"},{"label":"E","text":"Fibrinoid necrosis"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8ea449d7004c","stem":"A postmortem on the upper lobe of the right lung reveals the large triangle-like locus of the dark red dense tissue. Histological examination indicates necrosis of 22 the walls of the alveolus‘s and the lumens filled with erythrocytes. Which is the most likely associated finding? А. *Hemorrhagic infarct","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Histology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Carnification"},{"label":"C","text":"Lung‘s gangrene"},{"label":"D","text":"Hemorrhage"},{"label":"E","text":"Atelectasis"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Histology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-904debb7b4a1","stem":"A postmortem on an elderly male with atherosclerosis reveals a thrombus in a branch of the internal carotid artery as well as a grey locus of a moist softening of the brain‘s tissue. Which pathological process was found in the brain? А. *Ischemic infarct","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Neuroanatomy","topicOriginal":"Neuroanatomy","subtopic":"Brain","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Hemorrhagic infiltration"},{"label":"C","text":"Hematoma"},{"label":"D","text":"Encephalitis"},{"label":"E","text":"Tumor of a brain"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Neuroanatomy","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6bc504c3f7d4","stem":"A surgery on a patient, with a history of syphilis revealed a locus of flabby tis- sue. Grossly, this locus was yellowish, dry, structures and gummy. The most likely diagnoses is: А. *Caseous necrosis","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Infarct"},{"label":"C","text":"Waxy necrosis"},{"label":"D","text":"Fibrinoid a necrosis"},{"label":"E","text":"Steatonecrosis"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-70d5dd9efb68","stem":"The investigation of the liver‘s biopsy revealed that some separately arranged cells burn on small-sized pieces surrounded by a membrane. In some of them there were organelles, other had the fragments of dissolved nuclei. The inflammatory reaction around these cells missed. Name these changes: А. *Apoptosis","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Trauma and Emergency Surgery · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Trauma and Emergency Surgery","options":[{"label":"B","text":"Atrophy"},{"label":"C","text":"Necrosis"},{"label":"D","text":"Hypoplasia"},{"label":"E","text":"Dystrophy"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Trauma and Emergency Surgery · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9610520a01ce","stem":"An ill elderly patient with a atherosclerosis, develops pain in the left foot. Grossly was found the foot enlargement, its tissues were black, flabby and mace- rated. The demarcation zone was not expressed. Which term best characterized the foot tissues changes? А. * Moist (wet) gangrene.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Mummification."},{"label":"C","text":"Coagulate necrosis."},{"label":"D","text":"Dry gangrene."},{"label":"E","text":"Sequestrum."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a6c47f418d67","stem":"A 62-year-old female with atherosclerosis was admitted to the hospitalized. At surgery gross examination revealed purulent peritonitis. During the operation a 23 thrombus in the mesenteric arterias was found. Which was the most likely cause of the peritonitis? А. *Hemorrhagic infarct.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Abdominal Surgery · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Abdominal Surgery","options":[{"label":"B","text":"Angiospastic ischemia"},{"label":"C","text":"Ischemic infarct"},{"label":"D","text":"Stasis"},{"label":"E","text":"Compressive ischemia"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Abdominal Surgery · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-fc334a334d5b","stem":"The examination of a child, who had a history of measles, revealed reddish- black, uneven, swollen, slightly fluctuated lesions of cheaks and perineum area. Name the complication of measles? А. * Moist gangrene (noma)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Dry gangrene"},{"label":"C","text":"Gas gangrene"},{"label":"D","text":"Decubitus ulcer"},{"label":"E","text":"Trophic ulcer"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","fla